Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.92,0:17:00.88,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Yeah, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.54,0:17:02.95,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Wait, what's this about?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.04,0:17:04.96,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You're all staring as\Nthough you've seen a ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.04,0:17:07.18,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I know it's a funeral, and uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.22,0:17:10.05,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.20,0:17:11.68,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What's my name doing on there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.76,0:17:12.88,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm alive and well!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.08,0:17:14.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Wait, this funeral was for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.58,0:17:16.41,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Jojo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.49,0:17:18.39,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You're still recovering, you big silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.72,0:17:20.84,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Don't run off in the rain like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.78,0:17:26.26,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Here, take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.38,0:17:29.56,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Hey, that girl is Suzy Q.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.86,0:17:32.16,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And that ring looks like a...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.24,0:17:35.42,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me you don't\Nknow that we got married?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.80,0:17:37.34,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You got married?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.30,0:17:39.50,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Isn't it crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.74,0:17:41.00,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Just think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.36,0:17:42.72,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm officially Mrs.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.88,0:17:44.86,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Joseph Joestar. Goodness.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.30,0:17:49.18,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It makes me blush.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.20,0:17:51.80,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Wait a second here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.58,0:17:56.82,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Suzy Q, something about this doesn't\Nfeel right and I want to know what.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.16,0:18:00.90,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,The rock I was on fell into\Nthe ocean and me along with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.98,0:18:02.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,A fishing boat picked me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.86,0:18:04.24,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,So far, so good.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.58,0:18:08.96,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You nursed me back to health in Venice\Nfor two weeks, and we tied the knot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.04,0:18:11.22,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,So why did they all think I was dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.42,0:18:15.56,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You never sent that telegram\Nlike I asked, did you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.82,0:18:18.90,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Uh, I don't really know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.22,0:18:20.92,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,To me, that sounds like no.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.62,0:18:28.10,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Uh, now, now, let's not\Nget all clicky fingers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.90,0:18:30.52,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I never sent it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.72,0:18:31.86,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, JoJo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.70,0:18:33.68,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Ah! Suzy Q!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.04,0:18:35.00,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.20,0:18:37.38,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You had one job, woman! One job!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.22,0:18:40.05,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.13,0:18:41.94,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,JoJo came back to us all!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.92,0:18:43.75,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Stop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.83,0:18:45.52,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I said I was sorry! Sorry?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.72,0:18:47.13,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,They thought I was dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.44,0:18:50.27,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,JoJo.
Dialogue: 2,0:18:50.11,0:18:56.37,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,890)\be(2)}Elizabeth Joestar
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.44,0:18:53.08,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Soon after, Lisa Lisa, a .k .a.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.22,0:18:56.58,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Elizabeth Joestar, told JoJo\Nthat she was his mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.66,0:18:58.76,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,they moved to America.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.80,0:19:04.98,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,In 1948, she found love again and\Nmarried a Hollywood screenwriter.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:07.38,0:19:11.13,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,940)\be(2)}Erina Joestar
Dialogue: 2,0:19:08.17,0:19:11.13,Narrator,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Erina Joestar continued her work as a teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.40,0:19:11.38,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Iran Joestar continued\Nher work as a teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.22,0:19:16.20,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,In 1950, she died\Npeacefully at the age of 81,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.58,0:19:19.35,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,surrounded by family and\Nfriends who loved her.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:21.89,0:19:24.89,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,930)\be(2)}Robert E. O. Speedwagon
Dialogue: 2,0:19:22.60,0:19:27.85,Narrator,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Robert E. O. Speedwagon continued with his various enterprises
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.84,0:19:24.10,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Robert E .O.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.32,0:19:28.32,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Speedwagon continued to pour his\Nenergy into philanthropic research,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.60,0:19:31.94,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,helping to further science and\Nmedicine in countless ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.02,0:19:36.24,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,He died in 1952 of a heart\Nattack at 89 years of age.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.44,0:19:39.82,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,A lifelong bachelor, he\Nleft no family behind.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:40.49,0:19:45.66,Narrator,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Smokey Brown worked his way through college, majoring in political science.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.84,0:19:45.78,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Smokey Brown went on to work his way through\Ncollege, majoring in political science.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:41.91,0:19:45.66,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,940)\be(2)}Smokey Brown
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.20,0:19:51.79,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Later, he became the first black mayor\Nof a city in his home state of Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.26,0:19:56.70,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Major Rudolph von Stroheim\Nwould never see Jojo.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.78,0:20:00.82,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,again he died in 1943 at\Nthe battle of Stalingrad.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:57.18,0:19:59.30,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,930)\be(2)\fad(0,150)}Rudol von Stroheim
Dialogue: 2,0:19:57.18,0:19:59.30,Obituary2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,930)\be(2)\fad(0,150)}Rudolf von Stroheim
Dialogue: 2,0:19:57.18,0:20:04.85,Narrator,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}In 1943, he died as a proud German soldier, fighting in the Battle of Stalingrad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.90,0:20:03.86,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,A fearsome example of\Nthe German science he'd
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.94,0:20:07.02,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,always championed our\Ntechnology is the greatest.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.54,0:20:20.58,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And so the years flowed\Nby to a new generation.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:17.95,0:20:20.95,Title2.1,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,370)\pos(960,841)\bord3\blur2}JFK International Airport, New York, 1987
Dialogue: 1,0:20:17.95,0:20:20.95,Title2,Unknown,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,370)\pos(960,841)\be(2)}JFK International Airport, New York, 1987
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.72,0:20:24.02,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And as for JoJo...
